      "content": "It's possible that the platforms' algorithms are detecting patterns in your engagement that they interpret as spam or off-topic behavior, even if that isn't your intent. These systems sometimes analyze posting frequency, word choice, or topic shifts to categorize users. Instead of sensing a \"vibe,\" they are likely tracking measurable behavioral metrics that trigger moderation or reduced visibility. Try easing into interactions with shorter, more generalized comments for a while to gauge how the platforms react.",
