    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's exactly what i'm saying though. so it basically *is* a way of censoring specific types of people by labeling them as \"noise\" or \"deviant\" to the algorithm. if it's suppressing anything that's too novel or doesn't fit the baseline, isn't it essentially auto-isolating anyone who doesn't conform to the standard social frequency? it makes me think it's not just a bug, but a feature designed to keep people in these little predictable bubbles. is there any way to even test if this is a targeted suppression of certain personalities or \"frequencies\" rather than just a general moderation error?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
