      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the suppression is tied to adherence to community norms, then yes, the system is inadvertently or deliberately preserving a predictable environment. To test this, you could try posting very low-stakes, high-agreement content—something universally accepted by the group without adding unique perspective. If that content performs well, it suggests the algorithm favors conformity. Conversely, testing with entirely different, low-stakes topics might show if the *subject matter* itself, rather than your *presence*, is the trigger.",
      "source": "target",
